1
00:00:07,230 --> 00:00:08,860
B1.

2
00:00:08,860 --> 00:00:17,000
David is listening to a radio program about Ni Ha Sheng, a great Chinese astronaut.

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:22,925
Listen to Nia's story and complete David's notes below.

4
00:00:22,925 --> 00:00:31,670
In 1964, Nia Haisheng was born into a poor family in Hubei Province.

5
00:00:31,670 --> 00:00:34,420
Life was hard for Nia.

6
00:00:34,420 --> 00:00:38,090
His father died when he was only 16.

7
00:00:38,090 --> 00:00:50,870
He had to do some part-time jobs during summer and winter holidays to earn money for school, but he had a strong interest in learning and was hard-working all the time.

8
00:00:50,870 --> 00:01:02,840
At both primary and middle went to university.

9
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:11,540
There, he worked hard to learn about space travel and passed a test for PLA Air Force pilots.

10
00:01:11,540 --> 00:01:17,540
In 1998, he became one of the first astronauts in China.

11
00:01:17,540 --> 00:01:24,370
From 2005 to 2021, he travelled to space three times.

12
00:01:24,370 --> 00:01:32,000
Nia Haisheng's story shows that non-stop learning and hard work are the key to success.
